    "subtopic": "Area & volume formulas",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The perimeter of triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math> is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> inches, the length of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> inches, and the length of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> inches. What is the length, in inches, of side <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of all three sides of the triangle. It&rsquo;s given that the lengths of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow></math> and side <math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math> are <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> inches and <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> inches, respectively. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> represent the length, in inches, of side <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math>. The sum of the lengths, in inches, of all three sides of triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math> can be represented by the expression <math alttext=\"4 plus 7 plus x\"><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Since it&rsquo;s given that the perimeter of triangle <math alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math> is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn></math> inches, it follows that <math alttext=\"17 equals 4 plus 7 plus x\"><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"17 equals 11 plus x\"><mn>17</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"6 equals x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow></math>. Therefore, the length, in inches, of side <math alttext=\"upper B upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the length, in inches, of side <math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the lengths, in inches, of sides <math alttext=\"upper A upper B\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>B</mi>\n</mrow></math> and <math alttext=\"upper A upper C\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>A</mi>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n</mrow></math>.</p>",
