    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> of a rectangle is the product of its length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and its width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math>. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A upper B upper C upper D\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> has an area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280\"><mn>280</mn></math> square centimeters and the length of the rectangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280\"><mn>280</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"280 equals 10 w\"><mn>280</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>w</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28 equals w\"><mn>28</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>w</mi></math>. Therefore, the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the length, in centimeters, not the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This is half the area, in square centimeters, not the width, in centimeters, of the rectangle.</p>",
