    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "B",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The formula for the area, <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is <math alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the length of the base of the triangle and <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the triangle. It's given that the length of the base of a triangle is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> inches and the height of the triangle is <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn></math> inches. Substituting <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"12\"><mn>12</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals one half b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals one half left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis left parenthesis 12 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>8</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 48\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square inches, of the triangle is <math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum of the length of the base of the triangle and the height of the triangle, not the area of the triangle.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the product of the length of the base of the triangle and the height of the triangle, not the area of the triangle.</p>",
