    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each side of a square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn></math>. What is the perimeter of this square?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "180",
    "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn></math>. The perimeter of a polygon is equal to the sum of the lengths of the sides of the polygon. It&rsquo;s given that each side of the square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn></math>. Since a square is a polygon with <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> sides, the perimeter of this square is <math alttext=\"45 plus 45 plus 45 plus 45\"><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn></math>.</p>"
