    "subtopic": "Area & volume formulas",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Circle <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> has a radius of <math alttext=\"4 millimeters left parenthesis mm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>millimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>mm</mtext></mfenced></math>. Circle <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math> has an area of <math alttext=\"100 pi mm squared\"><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. What is the total area, <math alttext=\"in mm squared\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circles <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math>?</p>",
    "type": "mcq",
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The area, <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a circle is given by the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals pi r squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> represents the radius of the circle. It&rsquo;s given that circle <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> has a radius of <math alttext=\"4 millimeters left parenthesis mm right parenthesis\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mtext>millimeters</mtext><mo> </mo><mfenced><mtext>mm</mtext></mfenced></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> for <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals pi r squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper A equals pi left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis squared\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&pi;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"upper A equals 16 pi\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>&pi;</mi></math>. Therefore, the area of circle <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"16 pi mm Superscript 2\"><mn>16</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It&rsquo;s given that circle <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math> has an area of <math alttext=\"100 pi mm Superscript 2\"><mn>100</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mtext>mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the total area, <math alttext=\"in mm Superscript 2\"><msup><mtext>in mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of circles <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"16 pi plus 100 pi\"><mn>16</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>&pi;</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"116 pi\"><mn>116</mn><mi>&pi;</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum of the radii, <math alttext=\"in mm\"><mtext>in mm</mtext></math>, of circles <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math> multiplied by <math alttext=\"pi\"><mi>&pi;</mi></math>, not the total area, <math alttext=\"in mm Superscript 2\"><msup><mtext>in mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the circles.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the sum of the diameters, <math alttext=\"in mm\"><mtext>in mm</mtext></math>, of circles <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi></math> and <math alttext=\"upper L\"><mi>L</mi></math> multiplied by <math alttext=\"pi\"><mi>&pi;</mi></math>, not the total area, <math alttext=\"in mm Superscript 2\"><msup><mtext>in mm</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the circles.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors. </p>",
