    "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right prism has a square base with side lengths of <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> inches. The height of the prism is <math alttext=\"58\"><mn>58</mn></math> inches. What is the volume, in cubic inches, of the prism?</p>",
    "type": "grid-in",
    "correctAnswer": "5800",
    "explanation": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5,800\"><mn>5,800</mn></math>. The volume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, of a right prism with a square base is given by the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals s squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> is the side length of the square base and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height of the prism. It&rsquo;s given that a right prism has a square base with side lengths of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> inches. It's also given that the height of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"58\"><mn>58</mn></math> inches. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"58\"><mn>58</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals s squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals left parenthesis 10 right parenthesis squared left parenthesis 58 right parenthesis\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>58</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals 5,800\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5,800</mn></math>. Therefore, the volume, in cubic inches, of the prism is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5,800\"><mn>5,800</mn></math>.</p>"
